A bare func() is reserved only as a function/method result (a cleanup). A func()-typed
variable is an ordinary value: Hook satisfies NewServer’s func() input, while NewServer’s
own func() result is the aggregated cleanup. The two func() roles stay distinct.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Server struct{}

//plumb:build
var Hook = func() {}

//plumb:build
func NewServer(h func()) (*Server, func()) { return &Server{}, func() {} }
